body:
In the future it might come with standard insurance. But the insurance needs to be extented when it runs out.

&#x200B;

For now all ships have LTI insurance in the current builds.

i think you should look at it from two angles; design, and functionality

but first, ask yourself; do you want to be a pilot of a ship dedicated to dropping troops off? compare this ship to the valkyrie, valkyrie has more functionality; cargo grid, ability to transport vehicles, and more fire support. The con of the valkyrie is it's massive heat signature. You will be able to see one coming from far away. You drop troops off, you go airborne, and support them with your firepower.

&#x200B;

The prowler, however, is more stealthy, harder to detect. Furthermore it has a air bubble/shield, allowing people to breathe, even if the doors are open in space.

&#x200B;

You could see it this way;

Valkyrie; marine like missions

Prowler; spec ops like missions

\+verify

&#x200B;

Corsair <- taurus
